{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subject that broadcasts values to multiple consumers without storing a current value."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Unlike "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CurrentValueSubject"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PassthroughSubject"},{"text":" does not retain the most recent value.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This is an ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that allows multiple tasks to asynchronously consume values and mimics Combine’s PassthroughSubject.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"final"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"PassthroughSubject","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Subscribing","anchor":"Subscribing","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A consumer subscribes when its iterator is created, which is when a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for try await"},{"type":"text","text":" loop over the subject"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"(or over an operator chain built on it) begins. From then on, every value sent is buffered for that consumer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"until it is consumed, so a consumer that is slower than the sender still sees every value, in order.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Values sent while there are no subscribers are discarded; they are never replayed to a later consumer."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Starting a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"text":" that iterates the subject does not mean it has subscribed yet. If values must","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not be missed, subscribe before starting it: make the iterator now and hand it to the consumer as an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncIteratorSequence","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncIteratorSequence(subject.makeAsyncIterator())"},{"text":"). Or wait until the consumer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has subscribed before sending, for example with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"handleEvents(receiveMakeIterator:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Important","type":"aside"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cancelling a task waiting for the subject’s next value ends that consumer’s subscription; values sent afterwards"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are not delivered to it. To read the subject again, make a new iterator."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Example","anchor":"Example","type":"heading"},{"code":["let subject = PassthroughSubject<Int>()","let subscribed = SingleValueSubject<Void>()","","subject.send(0) \/\/ No subscribers yet, so this value is discarded.","","Task {","    for try await value in subject.handleEvents(receiveMakeIterator: { try? subscribed.send() }) {","        print(\"Received value: \\(value)\") \/\/ prints 1, then 2","    }","}","","try await subscribed.execute()","subject.send(1)","subject.send(2)","subject.send(completion: .finished)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PassthroughSubject","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTi